{:id :EACL-FORMAL-082
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace "eacl-rust BUGS.md EACL-RS-007 (rs007-acyclic, rs007-recursive)"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before strong-Kleene fault semantics"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "Reverse enumeration qualified every released scan row and threw on a fault before learning whether the row led to any resource. A faulting edge that reached no resource failed lookups and counts on both the least-path and first-discovery routes, while every point check answered no-permission."
 :fix
 "Faults are Kleene unknowns carried as path evidence. A row is joined with its continuation like any other row, so a faulting edge with no matching arrow target composes to false. Only a consumed candidate whose complete decision faults fails a page or count."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.datascript.kleene-fault-test/a-faulting-edge-that-reaches-no-resource-never-fails-a-walk"
  "eacl.datascript.kleene-fault-test/only-a-consumed-candidate-can-fail-a-page"
  "eacl.datascript.kleene-fault-test/a-faulting-subject-is-excluded-from-the-wildcard-and-fails-only-the-page-that-consumes-it"
  "eacl.datascript.caveat-context-admission-test/the-eacl-rust-context-type-repros-are-rejected-at-admission"
  "eacl.engine.least-path-evidence-test/legacy-node-evidence-is-bounded-and-demanded-faults-survive"
  "QualifiedEvidence.FaultsAreNotDecisive"
  "QualifiedEvidence.FoldsMustNotStopAtAFault"]
 :notes
 "The original repro faults through a context-type mismatch, which fail-fast admission now rejects before evaluation. The closing fixture uses a missing map key, which only evaluation can detect."}
